    base-offset probes (mov eax, imm32; ret) and compile-time field-offset asserts;
  * native-classes/NetworkReplicator2008StatsItem.cpp   create<ReplicatorStatsItem, shared_ptr<Replicator>,
                                                         RakNetStatistics*>, shared_ptr<ReplicatorStatsItem>(p, Deleter);
  * native-classes/NetworkReplicator2008AskAddChild.cpp Peer::askAddChild (dynamic_cast<const Replicator*>) and
                                                         Server::askAddChild (dynamic_cast<const ClientProxy*>), the two
                                                         bodies record_native_network_client_server2008.py leaves open.

Every row must be relocation-masked exact against the original, and every REL32/DIR32 target is bound to the address
the original instruction uses and verified: imports by DLL export name, type descriptors and vtables by original RTTI
names, own symbols by the row proven here, and the remaining externals by the EXTERNAL map (call sites read in the
original disassembly). A symbol binds to one address across all rows. No vtable is emitted by these units (asserted). The RTTI base lists of Replicator, ClientProxy and
ReplicatorStatsItem and the allocation sizes are checked against the binary. A row already counted by another receipt is
never counted here (checked at run time). Writes work/2008-06/shared-layouts/network-replicator2008-working.json.
