{"date": "2026-10-25", "title": "2008-06 SEH/switch bounds audit 10-25", "text": "Audit of unmatched rows with unaligned starts / out-of-extent jumps. Merged 12 parents via work/2008-06/bounds.json, each proven from binary tables: 9 _except_handler3 parents whose scope tables point past their end (00421f00 00422030 00422100 00422220 00422340 00422460 004328c0 00501400 00595a80: __finally/__except filter+handler belong to the same COFF function); 2 switch parents whose jump tables list the following rows (00486370 +0048668f,004866be; 005102d0 +005103b3); 0044b9a0 +0044baa2 (parent jne into it; catch(...) funclet mid-body). Retired 2 fake exacts (00501484, 00595ab8 = __except filter expressions). Rows 22303->22291. Existing sources: 00486370, 005102d0, 00501400 exact at new extents (net +1 exact, 21913). Parents of __finally tails now 71-95% (sources need real finally bodies: GetLastError/SetLastError state restore). Not changed: 41 bodies jumping into adjacent C++ catch eh rows (keep per __catch$ rule; tool should compare without inline funclets, e.g. 0046e430). Evidence/scripts: work/bounds-audit-20261025/."}
{"date": "2026-10-25", "title": "catch-funclet extents and funclet shapes (0040f9a0 exact)", "text": "0040f9a0 (ATL CreateInstance clone) was stuck 82-94% because the analyzer split its MSVC C++ catch funclet + common continuation into a separate pseudo-function (0040fa39, 38B) - the compared extent (153B) excluded them while the candidate extraction merges __catch$ blocks into the body. Fix: extend work/2008-06/bounds.json with the proven extent 191 so the target includes funclet+continuation, then re-analyze the client. Proof pattern for funclet extents: the pseudo-function starts with mov ecx,[ebp-N] dereferencing the OWNER frame without setting up ebp; it ends with mov eax,<continuation>; ret; the continuation restores the owner fs:[0] frame and rets with the owner's arg count; sibling CreateInstance clones share the family. With the full extent compared, the funclet shape becomes matchable: target 'mov ecx,[ebp-0x14]; call sym; mov eax,cont; ret' = a POINTER- or REFERENCE-typed catch whose body makes one thiscall (catch (Exception&) { exception.Delete(); } with a non-virtual member). A by-value catch (param homed at the slot) yields 'lea ecx,[ebp-0x14]' instead; by-value with user copy ctor puts the copy call in the funclet. Je/jmp displacements into the continuation shift with funclet size, so funclet instruction count matters. Also: existing EH near-miss clones (0040fe50/0040ff20 previously exact) now check 86% locally because the current extraction merges funclets into the body while their stored extents exclude them - same bounds.json fix applies (their funclets sit at extent+0), or re-verify on a harness where extraction splits."}
{"date": "2026-10-25", "title": "2008-06 catch-funclet extents 10-25 (10 exacts)", "text": "match.coff_functions folds __catch$ labels into the owner body, so any target extent that stops before its catch funclets can never match. Proof rule: an eh row belongs to the preceding code row when its catch_context.handler equals the __ehhandler$ address the parent pushes (push -1; push HANDLER); continuation eh rows directly after a proven funclet join too. Applied 51 such merges to work/2008-06/bounds.json (plus 005f5280 re-pinned 84->90); left 19 rows already pinned by older audits. No exact changed size. Exacts with unchanged stored sources: 004097c0 004166a0 00416ac0 0044cbb0 0044e5d0 00454c90 00465550 004cb8e0 004cc5e0 005f5280. Near: 0041d760 99 (eax/edx regalloc), 004186d0/004c8010/0046e430/005f8b60 98. 0046e430 residue: lea ecx,[edx+eax] vs add ecx,eax in the unchecked_fill arg (STL header/codegen); 30729/50727/O1 grids worse. Supersedes the 10-13 'never merge catch funclets' rule. Also: push sym (target) vs push 0 (candidate) in EH prologues is cosmetic (reloc masked both sides). Evidence: work/bounds-audit-20261025b/, work/residue-audit-20261025/."}
