{"date": "2026-10-13", "title": "G3D 6.09 Roblox 2008 edits (2008-06)", "text": "Tried: read fresh target diffs for the 90-99% G3D sources. Win32Window ctor and the GImage decoders all moved string members by +0x28 and grew the frame by 0x28. RTTI proves GImage::Error -> std::runtime_error -> std::exception, with CatchableType size 0x60; ctor 0x4728b0 = runtime_error(reason), reason +0x28, filename +0x44. Added recipe g3d-6.09-rbx2008 (header patches in roc/libs.py). libs.unit patched copies now redirect in-tree include dirs, and __FILE__ is restored to the pristine tree. Second edit: the inlined BinaryInput::getCArray throws std::exception (0x820c68 string, exception(const char* const&) import). Third: decodeJPEG sets jerr.error_exit = 0x50b530 (output_message, jpeg_destroy, format_message, throw runtime_error); generated unit roc_g3d_jpeg_throw_414d7d8a47fb28a0.cpp. Exacts gained (server-verified): 9 = 004728b0 004824f0 0050b700 0050bb30 0050cdd0 0050d800 0050ec40 0050fef0 0050cb40, plus 12 partial improvements. Local exact but blocked: 0050edb0 00510490 007b6c20 (server verifier still has the pre-getCArray libs.py: 'server already has this or better'); 00473790 and 00510586 are unknown to the server function table. Rejected/parked: 0053f160 (misattributed /Od dtor); 00486370 Shader (analyzer extent truncated, jumps leave the function); Sky funclets (2008 Sky has a 4x0x18 array vs upstream 6x4; layout not yet proven); ATL CComObject and EnumDesc targets are misattributed. Next: restart the verifiers, resubmit 0050edb0 00510490 007b6c20, then submit what the background 'roc libs g3d-6.09-rbx2008' sweep saved (stage events touched 004737b0, Texture, VARArea, GCamera, BinaryInput). Derive the 2008 Sky layout from Sky::fromFile/~Sky."}
